# Nothing here is line-ending normalised. Git stores every file byte for byte,
# and checks it out byte for byte.
#
# This is deliberate, not neglect. Five files in this repository are CRLF and
# have to stay CRLF: src/glview.cpp, src/nifskope.cpp, src/gl/controllers.cpp,
# src/spells/havok.cpp and WW_CHANGES.md. Everything else is LF. Without the
# line below, a clone made with Git for Windows' default core.autocrlf=true
# rewrites them on checkout, and the next commit is a 33,000-line diff that
# changes no code.
#
# The previous contents of this file were `*.cpp eol=auto` and friends, which
# is not a value git recognises. It did nothing; the repository only survived
# on core.autocrlf=false being set locally, which a contributor will not have.
* -text
